{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "washtenaw-county",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.3.45, step 7f: Washtenaw's COMPLETE County Data Manager database, as the onroad chain mounts it -- `washtenaw_cdb` as `characterization/county-inputs/washtenaw-county/setup-county.sql` builds it for `scale-county`. Unlike the two `-single` databases beside it (`washtenaw-county-starts`, `washtenaw-county-hotelling`), which hold only what their off-network runs read and skip MOVES's domain-database validation, this one holds every table the County Data Manager's importers require of a running-exhaust run, and every row in it is a `CREATE TABLE ... LIKE` + `INSERT ... SELECT` copy of the default database's own rows at county 26161, zone 261610, year 2020 and fuel region 270000000 (whole tables where there is no such key). Two rows are not copies and neither is a model input: `avft`, AVFTTool's default projection of `sampleVehiclePopulation`, after which the execution database's `sampleVehiclePopulation` is still the default's; and `auditLog`'s \"No I/M Program\" flag, which only the validation reads.\n\nTHE MERGE (conventions §100), measured as the diff of `scale-county`'s execution database against its DEFAULT-domain twin `expand-roadtypes` (same county, year, month, hour and vehicle): every table the model reads is identical at every row but five, and those five are MOVES's SINGLE-scale REPLACEs -- `sourceTypeYear`, `sourceTypeAgeDistribution`, `HPMSVtypeYear` hold the 2020 rows alone, which are the rows read, and `fuelSupply`, `IMCoverage` hold the county's fuel region and nothing -- so they are the default's (§92). The other differences are the run's own selection of extended idle (9190, which a passenger car never emits) and the bundle bookkeeping. So this document declares the same input sides the `-single` ones do and no more: `zone` and `zoneRoadType` SHADOW the default's rows with the default's own values, bit for bit, so `zn_mergedStartAllocFactor` and `zrt_mergedSHOAllocFactor` return the default's; `hotellingActivityDistribution` at zone 261610 is empty, so the default's 990000 rows merge untouched; the four other hotelling tables and `startsPerDay` are empty (the county states starts as `startsPerDayPerVehicle`, the default's 26 rows, so AdjustStarts takes its population x startsPerDayPerVehicle arm, as at DEFAULT scale).\n\nIT DOES NOT LOAD ALONE: it names no runspec.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "onroad",
      "domain",
      "single-county-domain",
      "scale-input-database"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_link": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/Link.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_link"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "output",
          "domain"
        ],
        "note": "Link, the default database's national table: MOVES merges it into every domain but PROJECT (InputDataManager.java:1432), so a SINGLE-county run reads the same 22,610 synthetic links a DEFAULT one does, and selects county 26161's on-network and off-network ones by its joins.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_linksourcetypehour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/linkSourceTypeHour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_linksourcetypehour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "domain",
          "activity"
        ],
        "note": "linkSourceTypeHour, the default database's: 0 rows, and the county database has none. Only ProjectTAG reads it.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecdomain": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./washtenaw-county/runspecdomain.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecdomain"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
